At Mon,  8 Apr 2013 13:53:44 -0400,
mengdong.lin@intel.com wrote:
> 
> From: Mengdong Lin <mengdong.lin@intel.com>
> 
> A new function snd_hda_bus_reset() is defined to suspend and resume all codecs
> on the hda bus.

You mixed up the result and the purpose in the description :)

The purpose of snd_hda_bus_reset() is to reset the codecs on the bus,
and eventually this is implemented as temporary suspend-and-resume
calls as an ad hoc solution.

> It will be called by bus reset ops azx_bus_reset() as a rescue
> of codec communitation error.
> 
> snd_hda_suspend & snd_hda_resume will no longer be called by azx_bus_reset.
> So snd_hda_resume will only be used in system resume and may delay resuming a
> codec.

And write why this movement is needed.


Takashi


